    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0801" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/26787½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the President’s Personal Representative to
                        Pope Pius XII</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Taylor</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-12">December 12,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Apostolic Delegate<anchor n="51" xml:id="d684-f1"/> telephoned me this
                    morning and I called upon him. He has a further inquiry from the Vatican in
                    respect to the question of bombing Rome, indicating impatience at the Vatican
                    because we have not definitely communicated to the Holy See the suggestions
                    which you and Archbishop Spellman<anchor n="52" xml:id="d684-f2"/> and myself
                    have discussed with the President. He is indicating in his reply that the matter
                    is receiving active attention requiring consultation with the Allied Command and
                    the British. I made no definite statement but did express the hope that some
                    policy might be evolved, but whatever it is, future conduct would have to be
                    governed by the eventualities of the war, and further that Italy should not
                    provoke such an attack by any act of her own.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">yron</hi>] C. T[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">aylor</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d684-f1" n="51" xml:id="d684-f1-content">
                <p>Archbishop Amleto Giovanni Cicognani.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d684-f2" n="52" xml:id="d684-f2-content">
                <p>Francis Joseph Spellman, Archbishop of New York.</p>
